<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gorno-Badakhshan Autonomous Region</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gorno-Badakhshan, Gorno-Badakhshan Autonomous Oblast</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gorno-Badakhshan is an autonomous region of eastern Tajikistan covering the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamir-mountains">Pamir Mountains</a>, almost half of the country's area but with a small population. Created as an autonomous oblast in 1925, it is home to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamiris">Pamiri peoples</a>, who speak Eastern Iranian languages and mostly follow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismailism">Ismaili</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>. Its capital is Khorog, and it was an opposition stronghold in the civil war of 1992–1997.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gorno-badakhshan-autonomous-region.jpg" alt="Gorno-Badakhshan Autonomous Region" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zack Knowles · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_of_Khorog_from_the_Botanical_Gardens.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
